/T ("It worked," she agreed. "For a while. But fixing one collapse meant learning to see the shape of every collapse after it, and once a man learns to see that shape, he can't stop seeing it. Reset two came from a different Aiden Kade, in a different life the first reset had made possible, trying to prevent a different catastrophe he was no longer willing to let happen the ordinary way either. And then a third. And then people like Voss started noticing what the machine could do, and started wanting to hold it themselves.")
